uh what did you make of it Mr Stevenson  good morning  well I think the Prime Minister finished  the conference on a high we've got to  acknowledge there's been a bit of a  difficult few days for her but I think  she finished in a high and most  importantly of all she was setting out a  very strong policy agenda one which I  think all conservative MPS will  certainly get behind and I think it's an  extremely important agenda for people  such as myself who live in the north of  England where we've obviously been  advocating the leveling up agenda for  some time it's a Manifesto commitment  from 2019 and I feel very confident that  she's committed to it  did you vote for her  uh no I didn't but I don't think that's  relevant now what we've got to do is get  behind our prime minister we had uh an  election uh We've chosen our prime  minister uh she is now leading the party  and I think she's setting out a very  clear agenda one that clearly divides us  from opposition parties because you've  got people like the greens who don't  want to see growth in the economy  liberal Democrats never sure what  they're up to and labor who are devoid  of ideas we now have a clear agenda and  from the northern perspective we've long  said what is leveling up about it's two  things it's about improving people's  lives and it's about closing the gap  between those less prosperous areas with  the more prosperous areas and that means  growing our economy so I want to see the  policies that will lead to Greater  growth in the north of England we can  close that Gap  and does that include slashing the 45p  rate of tax and also Bankers bonuses  caps being removed  I think at the end of the day they were  a distraction to what we want to  actually achieve and I'm actually very  pleased the government to put that to  one side we can then concentrate on the  agenda and the policies that will  actually deliver the growth in the  places I want to see it so you're  cutting National Insurance I think is a  positive but it's not just about tax  cuts it's also about looking at the  amount of Regulation that there is and  it's looking at public sector investment  and skills in infrastructure and  attracting the private sector which  ultimately is the gold private sector  will lead to greater wealth creation  greater wealth creation leads to better  Public Services which is what something  which we all want to see okay so you you  also think it's a good idea to remove  the cap on Bankers bonuses then  well that's a private sector matter and  to be perfectly honest if we gain more  tax from that we can then use that tax  to pay for public services but what is  most important is about growing the  economy in different parts of the  country I want to see the economy of  this north of England close the gap with  some more successful Parts I want to see  other parts of the country continue to  be successful but we do need to see the  north grow as well okay if it's a  private sector matter why was it brought  up in the mini budget  well I think what's more important is  about looking at the policies that we're  going to take us forward that will grow  the economy in the north of England and  I think I think I know that's not my  question Mr Stevenson my question is  about Bankers bonuses you say it's a  private sector Master quite clearly  isn't because it was the government that  put the cap on there and I'm asking you  what impact that has on leveling up and  what your constituencies constituents  think about it  well I think it'll have a limited impact  on leveling up because I think leveling  up is about seeing the investment in the  north of England and other parts of the  country because we obviously want to see  the whole country uh level up and I  think it's the policies that will drive  that that are far more important it's  about increasing infrastructure  improvements it's about seeing skills  Improvement and it's about seeing uh  private sector being attracted to those  areas so that they can grow those vocal  economies see productivity increases  because it's through productivity  increase that you see how Society  increases wealth  so I'm sorry just to clarify are you  saying that you don't mind that cap  being lifted  I don't think it will have any great  impact on what we are trying to achieve  which is about growing the economy my  question Mr Stevenson just answer my  question if you would please do you  agree with uh Bankers bonuses cap being  lifted or not  I do not personally have a problem with  that  okay do you think that the people that  are your constituents that are  struggling to make ends meet will feel  the same way  I think people who I represent want to  see the local economy grow they want to  see investment into our area they want  to see their own individual lives  improve and that is what the gender that  the government is pursuing is all about  I want to see the Carlisle economy and  indeed the national economy improve I  want to see the standard of living with  the people in my area improve I want to  see the opportunities they have improve  and that is about investment and you are  starting to see that in places like  Carlisle we have investment going into  our University we have investment going  into our road infrastructure those are  the things that will improve the  productivity of the local economy and  therefore improve the lives the people  who live in my constituency okay the  good people of Carlisle won't carry  George that Bankers can get even bigger  bonuses than they did before  they all have different opinions on that  subject but I think far more importantly  people will be looking to what matters  in their own individual lives their own  communities and ultimately they want to  see the whole country succeed but I want  to concentrate on the policies that will  lead to an improved economy in Carlisle  and in other parts of the country yeah  the reason I'm asking you is of course  because Carlisle was a red wall State  until 2010 and it's exactly seats like  that that will have an opinion on uh  Bankers bonuses in the cap being lifted  and when they get into the polling booth  in 2022 December 2022 that could swing  it for them this government looking as  though they're looking after the fat  cats rather than leveling up in Carlisle  I disagree with that because I think  you're actually seeing direct investment  from government into places like  Carlisle I've already highlighted we've  got a Ring Road potential investment  we've got the university expanding in  the area we've seen job creation in the  area and I think what will matter to the  people of Carlisle at the next election  is has Carlisle improved has their own  individual lives improved and has the  opportunities for their own children and  families improved because that's a  critical thing I want to see everybody  improve their lives have greater  opportunity better jobs higher wages  greater productivity in the economy and  also our environment where they live and  their communities are prosperous that is  the policy of the present government  pursuing a growth agenda I think is the  right approach  uh that also I'm guessing I'd be  thinking about whether they can keep a  roof over their heads or even if they  can because mortgages have gone up so  high uh keep the heating on uh because  of increases uh in inflation the cost of  living and indeed mortgage rates because  this government was in danger of  crushing the economy  I don't think anybody disagrees that  there's good to be a difficult few  months I'm quite optimistic about things  I think inflation will drop  substantially next year interest rates  are rising not unique to the United  Kingdom interest rates are rising right  across the Europe and other parts of the  world I think they will ultimately  stabilize uh hopefully as the economy  recovers next year and you see inflation  drop that  interest rates will start to drop and  George we've also got to remember the  government has stepped in to support  families and businesses up and down the  country with the energy support that  they are giving Which is very very  substantial what I'd like to see  obviously is Energy prices generally  drop inflation drop in the car economy  start to grow as strongly and I think we  will see that next year yeah we all want  that to happen how high do you think  inflation is going to go before that  I'm not somebody who can predict these  things uh but I he just did predict that  it was going to go down I did yes but  not a specific figure uh what I did say  I think they will go down next year and  I think that will improve their people's  prospects okay it's good to talk to you  thanks very much indeed for joining us

